From 0daa3d3feb588871e54ff63050b063b4c9033644 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 11:55:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Hangfire recurring job registration: use
 IRecurringJobManager, not the static RecurringJob helper

Real bug, not a config issue. RecurringJob.AddOrUpdate<T>(...) is
Hangfire's legacy static-API convenience, and it depends on the global
JobStorage.Current being set. builder.Services.AddHangfire(config =>
config.UseMemoryStorage()) only configures Hangfire's DI-based services -
it never assigns that legacy global, which is exactly what "Current
JobStorage instance has not been initialized yet" means. The static call
was also failing purely because of *when* it ran: it executes before
app.RunAsync() starts the hosted services AddHangfireServer() registers,
so even if something else set the global later, it wouldn't have been
set yet at this point in Main either way.

Fixed by resolving IRecurringJobManager from the same service provider
AddHangfire(...) populated (app.Services.GetRequiredService<IRecurringJobManager>())
and calling AddOrUpdate on that instance instead of the static class -
this uses the storage that was actually configured, with no dependency
on a global assignment or hosted-service startup ordering. Exactly what
the exception's own message recommends.

No dotnet SDK in the authoring environment. Verified by brace balance
and a targeted check that IRecurringJobManager is the only new symbol
introduced, already covered by the existing 'using Hangfire;' (confirmed
via the exception's own stack trace, which shows Hangfire.RecurringJobManager
implementing this interface in the same root Hangfire namespace).
---
 invetoryBackGroundServices/Program.cs | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/invetoryBackGroundServices/Program.cs b/invetoryBackGroundServices/Program.cs
index 62459a5..0028030 100644
--- a/invetoryBackGroundServices/Program.cs
+++ b/invetoryBackGroundServices/Program.cs
@@ -285,7 +285,14 @@ namespace invetoryBackGroundServices
                 await startupJob.RunAsync();
             }
 
-            RecurringJob.AddOrUpdate<OutboxReconciliationJob>(
+            // The static RecurringJob.AddOrUpdate helper relies on the legacy global
+            // JobStorage.Current, which AddHangfire(...)'s DI-based registration never sets -
+            // that mismatch is exactly what "Current JobStorage instance has not been
+            // initialized yet" means. IRecurringJobManager, resolved from the same service
+            // provider AddHangfire populated, uses the storage that was actually configured
+            // instead of a global that nothing here ever assigns.
+            IRecurringJobManager recurringJobManager = app.Services.GetRequiredService<IRecurringJobManager>();
+            recurringJobManager.AddOrUpdate<OutboxReconciliationJob>(
                 "outbox-reconciliation", job => job.RunAsync(CancellationToken.None), Cron.MinuteInterval(30));
 
             await app.RunAsync();
